      "description": "Current vacancies, La Trobe University Existing application login Jobs at La Trobe Jobs home Current vacancies Working at La Trobe Overseas applicants Our employment strategies Recent Jobs Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Job Location Date Closes Senior Officer, Customer Care (ASK La Trobe) Melbourne (Bundoora) 20 Sep 2026 Work collaboratively within the team and as a member of the ASK La Trobe to facilitate efficient and effective customer service delivery to students and administrative support staff in the University. Casual Campaign - Student Ambassador ASK La Trobe Bendigo, Melbourne (Bundoora) 20 Sep 2026 Support new students by answering study and campus enquiries, assisting with orientation planning, providing LMS and Handbook guidance, making referrals, and handling inbound and outbound student communications. Community Engagement and Co-Production Coordinator, Australian Autism Knowledge Hub Melbourne (Bundoora) 16 Sep 2026 Support meaningful community engagement and co-production, ensuring the voices, knowledge and priorities of the autism community shape the Hub’s research, training and knowledge translation. Senior Analytics Engineer Melbourne (Bundoora) 6 Sep 2026 Shape the future of data-driven decision making at La Trobe\nFull-time, Continuing Melbourne (Bundoora Campus) / Hybrid Senior Manager, Data and Analytics Engineering Melbourne (Bundoora) 6 Sep 2026 Lead the next chapter of Data & Analytics at La Trobe University Research Fellow Melbourne (Bundoora) 6 Sep 2026 Help shape the future of HIV care! Join our pilot project co-designing a new model to integrate PozQoL across clinical, community and peer services. Expressions of Interest Animal Ethics Committee - Category A- veterinary surgeon Melbourne (Bundoora) 6 Sep 2026 La Trobe University is seeking expressions of interest for a Category A member—an experienced or knowledgeable veterinary surgeon—to join its Animal Ethics Committee, which oversees the ethical use of animals in research and teaching in compliance with national codes and legislation. This role involves reviewing research proposals, attending monthly meetings, participating in facility inspections, and ensuring animal welfare is prioritised, with appropriate training, support, and reimbursement provided. Team Lead/Senior Counsellor, Bundoora Counselling Services Melbourne (Bundoora) 7 Sep 2026 Lead a dedicated team delivering high-quality mental health and well-being support, fostering a safe, inclusive counselling service that supports student success and well-being. Associate Director, Research Development & Grants Melbourne (Bundoora) 13 Sep 2026 Lead La Trobe University's research funding growth agenda, driving grant development, strategic partnerships and researcher capability to secure nationally and internationally competitive funding outcomes. Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest Campus Independent Indigenous Australian candidates; register your Expression of Interest here to receive regular job vacancy information at La Trobe University. General Expressions Of Interest Senior Officer, Customer Care (ASK La Trobe) Work collaboratively within the team and as a member of the ASK La Trobe to facilitate efficient and effective customer service delivery to students and administrative support staff in the University. More details... Casual Campaign - Student Ambassador ASK La Trobe Support new students by answering study and campus enquiries, assisting with orientation planning, providing LMS and Handbook guidance, making referrals, and handling inbound and outbound student communications. More details... Expressions of Interest Animal