    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/570722/senior-analytics-engineer": {
      "title": "Details",
      "description": "Details - Senior Analytics Engineer, La Trobe University Existing application login Jobs at La Trobe Jobs home Current vacancies Working at La Trobe Overseas applicants Our employment strategies Details - Senior Analytics Engineer Senior Analytics Engineer Job No.: 570722 Work type: Continuing La Trobe University is embarking on an exciting transformation of its data and analytics capabilities. We're seeking a highly skilled Senior Analytics Engineer to help build the trusted, scalable and analytics-ready data products that support decision-making across the University. Working within a modern Azure, Databricks and dbt environment, you'll play a critical role in designing robust data models, developing semantic layers and delivering high-quality data assets that enable reporting, analytics and emerging AI initiatives. This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced analytics engineering professional who enjoys solving complex problems, influencing technical standards and mentoring others while remaining hands-on with technology. About the position Reporting to the Senior Manager, Data & Analytics Engineering, you will: Design, develop and own scalable Gold-layer data products, semantic models and analytics-ready data assets that support enterprise decision-making. Build and optimise semantic layers that support enterprise reporting and self-service analytics. Collaborate with data engineers, analysts and business stakeholders to translate requirements into effective solutions. Champion best-practice data modelling, testing, documentation and governance standards. Mentor junior team members and contribute technical leadership across the analytics engineering capability. Support the delivery of innovative analytics and AI-ready solutions that create value for the University community. Act as a technical authority for analytics engineering, establishing modelling standards, reusable patterns and quality practices across the University. Skills and experience To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Significant experience delivering enterprise data and analytics solutions. Advanced expertise in SQL, dimensional modelling and analytics engineering practices. Experience working with modern cloud data platforms such as Azure, Databricks and dbt. Strong understanding of data governance, metadata, lineage and data quality principles. Excellent stakeholder engagement and communication skills. The ability to work independently while contributing positively to a collaborative team environment. HEO9 Senior Analytics Engineer (4).docx Benefits include: Flexible work arrangements Generous leave provisions Professional development opportunities Access to health and wellbeing initiatives A collaborative and inclusive culture View all benefits: http://www.latrobe.edu.au/jobs/working/benefits Welcome to Bundoora La Trobe's Melbourne (Bundoora) campus is home to a vibrant community of staff and students and sits within one of Australia's largest university campuses, offering modern facilities, excellent public transport access and a strong connection to industry and community partners. Closing Date: By 11:55pm on 6 September Recruitment enquiries: Senior Talent Acquisition Partner, Strategy and Senior Appointments m.magaton@latrobe.edu.au Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up-to-date resume; and cover letter Please scroll down to apply. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation of liberty or autonomy. Why La Trobe Develop your career at an innovative, global university where you’ll collaborate with community and industry to create impact. Enjoy working on our inspiring and stunning campuses – the perfect hub for industry, students and academics. Help transform the lives of students, partners and communities now and in the future. Advertised: 23/8/2026 Closing Date: 06/9/2026 Back to search results Apply now Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Job Location Date Closes Senior Analytics Engineer Melbourne (Bundoora) 6 Sep 2026 