    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/570824/senior-manager-data-and-analytics-engineering": {
      "title": "Details",
      "description": "Details - Senior Manager, Data and Analytics Engineering, La Trobe University Existing application login Jobs at La Trobe Jobs home Current vacancies Working at La Trobe Overseas applicants Our employment strategies Details - Senior Manager, Data and Analytics Engineering Senior Manager, Data and Analytics Engineering Job No.: 570824 Work type: Continuing Data & Analytics Full-time, Continuing Melbourne (Bundoora Campus) / Hybrid La Trobe University is seeking an experienced and visionary leader to drive the future of our Data & Analytics Engineering capability. As Senior Manager, Data & Analytics Engineering, you will lead a team responsible for the platforms, standards and engineering practices that underpin trusted analytics and data-informed decision making across the University. You will shape strategic direction, build organisational capability and ensure our enterprise data platform supports current and future business needs. This is an influential leadership opportunity for someone who combines strong technical credibility with the ability to inspire teams, engage senior stakeholders and deliver strategic outcomes. About the position Reporting into senior technology leadership, you will: Lead and develop multidisciplinary Data Engineering and Analytics Engineering teams responsible for the University's enterprise data platform and analytics capabilities. Develop and implement the strategic roadmap for analytics engineering capabilities and platforms. Establish and maintain robust data architecture, governance and engineering standards. Lead a high-performing team of technical specialists, fostering a culture of collaboration, innovation and continuous improvement. Partner with leaders across the University to understand strategic priorities and deliver impactful data solutions. Oversee platform performance, sustainability, security and operational excellence. Support the University's analytics, reporting and AI ambitions through modern, scalable data platforms. Ensure the enterprise data platform remains secure, reliable, scalable and cost-effective while supporting current and future analytics and AI use cases. Skills and experience To be successful in this role, you will bring: Significant leadership experience within data, analytics or technology environments. Demonstrated success leading high-performing technical teams. Experience delivering enterprise-scale data platform and analytics initiatives. Strong knowledge of cloud-based data ecosystems, analytics engineering practices and governance frameworks. Outstanding stakeholder engagement and influencing skills, including experience working with senior executives. The ability to translate strategic objectives into practical and sustainable outcomes. Why La Trobe Develop your career at an innovative, global university where you’ll collaborate with community and industry to create impact. Enjoy working on our inspiring and stunning campuses – the perfect hub for industry, students and academics. Help transform the lives of students, partners and communities now and in the future. Benefits include: Flexible work arrangements Generous leave provisions Access to professional learning and leadership development Health and wellbeing programs A supportive and collaborative workplace culture View all benefits: http://www.latrobe.edu.au/jobs/working/benefits HEO10 Senior Manager Data and Analytics Engineering (4).docx Welcome to Bundoora La Trobe's Melbourne (Bundoora) campus is home to a vibrant community of staff and students and sits within one of Australia's largest university campuses, offering modern facilities, excellent public transport access and a strong connection to industry and community partners. Closing Date: By 11:55pm on 6 September Recruitment enquiries: Senior Talent Acquisition Partner, Strategy and Senior Appointments m.magaton@latrobe.edu.au Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up-to-date resume; and cover letter Please scroll down to apply. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation of liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 23/8/2026 Closing Date: 06/9/2026 Back to search results Apply now Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Job Location Date Closes Senior Manager, Data and Analytics Engineering Melbourne (Bundoora) 6 Sep 2026 Lead the next chapter of Data & Analytics at La Trobe University General Expressions Of Interest Senior Officer, Customer Care (ASK La Trobe) Work collaboratively within the team and as a member of the ASK La Trobe to facilitate efficient and effective customer service delivery to students and administrative support staff in the University. More details... Casual Campaign - Student Ambassador ASK La Trobe Support new students by answering study and campus enquiries, assisting with orientation planning, providing LMS and Handbook guidance, making referrals, and handling inbound and outbound student communications. More details... Expressions of Interest Animal Ethics Committee - Category A- veterinary surgeon La Trobe University is seeking expressions of interest for a Category A member—an experienced or knowledgeable veterinary surgeon—to join its Animal Ethics Committee, which oversees the ethical use of animals in research and teaching in compliance with national codes and legislation. This role involves reviewing research proposals, attending monthly meetings, participating in facility inspections, and ensuring animal welfare is prioritised, with appropriate training, support, and reimbursement provided. More details... Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest Indigenous Australian candidates; register your Expression of Interest here to receive regular job vacancy information at La Trobe University. More details... Current Opportunities Job Closes Senior Manager, Data and Analytics Engineering 6 Sep 2026 Lead the next chapter of Data & Analytics at La Trobe University Powered by PageUp To perform a job search, select your preferred job criteria below. Job search Work Type Continuing 1 Location Australia Melbourne (Bundoora) 1 Category Classification Level - Professional HEO10 1 Professional Business Analysis 1 Want to know more? Recruitment contacts T: +61 (0)3 9479 1234 F: +61 (0)3 9471 0369 Jobs for students Jobs for staff [Restricted] Facebook Twitter Youtube Linked in Instagram Emergency information Contacts Site map Accessibility Privacy Copyright and disclaimer © Copyright 2014 La Trobe University. All rights reserved. CRICOS Provider Code: VIC 00115M"
