    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/571024/steam-curriculum-operations-manager": {
      "title": "STEAM Curriculum & Operations Manager, La Trobe University",
      "description": "Details - STEAM Curriculum & Operations Manager, La Trobe University Existing application login Jobs at La Trobe Jobs home Current vacancies Working at La Trobe Overseas applicants Our employment strategies Details - STEAM Curriculum & Operations Manager STEAM Curriculum & Operations Manager Job No.: 571024 Work type: Continuing Full Time, Continuing Position based at Bendigo Campus HEO8 salary range $119,264 – $136,382 plus 17% superannuation Relocation reimbursement of up to $5000, if outside Bendigo About the position Bendigo Tech School is part of the Victorian Government’s commitment to developing enterprise capabilities needed by young people to leverage opportunities in the overlapping fields of Science, Technology, Engineering, Arts and Mathematics (STEAM). Our mission is to build students’ enterprise capabilities to increase their job prospects by enhancing their skills in the areas of digital technologies, critical and creative thinking, communication, analytics, planning, problem-solving, self-management, and collaboration. The STEAM Curriculum & Operations Manager is the senior internal delivery lead for Bendigo Tech School. The role is responsible for coordinating the end-to-end design, scheduling, quality assurance, operational readiness, and continuous improvement of Bendigo Tech School’s learning programs. To hold this La Trobe University position the occupant must hold current Teacher Registration with the Victorian Institute of Teaching. with this specific link : https://www.vit.vic.edu.au/register/legislation Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have; A degree in Education or a relevant STEAM discipline with substantial experience in curriculum design, program leadership, and educational operations; postgraduate study or equivalent experience highly regarded. Ability to develop innovative STEAM programs using advanced technologies and contemporary pedagogy. Ability to be responsible for the delivery of educational programs. Demonstrated management and leadership skills with experience in managing and leading staff to promote a cohesive and effective team and managing workflows. Proven experience and success in managing staff performance and development. Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. PD - STEAM Curriculum and Operations Manager.pdf Benefits 17% employer contributed superannuation Private Health Insurance discount Plus, many more, click HERE How to apply Closing date:  By 11:55pm Sunday 11 th October 2026 Position Enquiries: Luke Chandler, Director Bendigo Tech School Email: Luke.Chandler@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: recruitment@latrobe.edu.au Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: A cover letter, outlining why you are interested and what skills and experience you bring to the role. An up-to-date resume. Please scroll down to apply. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005.  If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 13/9/2026 Closing Date: 11/10/2026 Back to search results Apply now Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Job Location Date Closes STEAM Curriculum & Operations Manager Bendigo 11 Oct 2026 Provide leadership across the full program lifecycle, from initial curriculum and program design through to scheduling, delivery, evaluation and continuous improvement. General Expressions Of Interest Casual Instructional Coaching Role – Momentum CoachED program Join the Momentum CoachED program as an instructional coach, providing one-on-one support that helps teachers strengthen practice and improve student learning. More details... Senior Officer, Customer Care (ASK La Trobe) Work collaboratively within the team and as a member of the ASK La Trobe to facilitate efficient and effective customer service delivery to students and administrative support staff in the University. More details... Casual Campaign - Student Ambassador ASK La Trobe Support new students by answering study and campus enquiries, assisting with orientation planning, providing LMS and Handbook guidance, making referrals, and handling inbound and outbound student communications. More details... Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest Indigenous Australian candidates; register your Expression of Interest here to receive regular job vacancy information at La Trobe University. More details... Current Opportunities Job Closes STEAM Curriculum & Operations Manager 11 Oct 2026 Provide leadership across the full program lifecycle, from initial curriculum and program design through to scheduling, delivery, evaluation and continuous improvement. Powered by PageUp To perform a job search, select your preferred job criteria below. Job search Work Type Continuing 1 Location Australia Bendigo 1 Category Professional Education and Training 1 Educational Services 1 Want to know more? Recruitment contacts T: +61 (0)3 9479 1234 F: +61 (0)3 9471 0369 Jobs for students Jobs for staff [Restricted] Facebook Twitter Youtube Linked in Instagram Emergency information Contacts Site map Accessibility Privacy Copyright and disclaimer © Copyright 2014 La Trobe University. All rights reserved. CRICOS Provider Code: VIC 00115M"
