    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/570949/cisco-chair-for-ai-in-health-systems": {
      "title": "Cisco Chair for AI in Health Systems",
      "description": "Details - Cisco Chair for AI in Health Systems, La Trobe University Existing application login Jobs at La Trobe Jobs home Current vacancies Working at La Trobe Overseas applicants Our employment strategies Details - Cisco Chair for AI in Health Systems Cisco Chair for AI in Health Systems Job No.: 570949 Work type: Fixed Term Rare opportunity to Shape the Future of AI-Enabled Healthcare Join La Trobe University and Cisco in a flagship leadership role driving AI innovation, healthcare transformation and industry partnership at a national and international level. Full Time / Fixed Term / Research Only Appointment Until 31.07.2029 / Bundoora Campus About the position La Trobe University is seeking an outstanding research and innovation leader to join one of Australia's most successful university-industry collaborations. The Cisco Chair for AI in Health Systems is a flagship appointment established through the long-standing partnership between La Trobe University and Cisco, bringing together world-leading expertise in artificial intelligence, healthcare innovation, industry engagement and research translation. The role will provide national and international leadership in AI-enabled health systems, driving real-world impact through pioneering research, strategic partnerships and industry collaboration. Reporting to the Dean and working across the Cisco-La Trobe Centre for AI and IoT, Innovation Central Melbourne and a broad network of healthcare, industry and government partners, you will accelerate the translation of AI research into scalable solutions that improve patient outcomes, transform healthcare delivery and deliver meaningful societal impact. Duties at this level: Provide strategic leadership in AI-enabled health systems and drive the translation of research into real-world healthcare innovation. Build and lead multidisciplinary research collaborations spanning universities, healthcare providers, government and industry. Attract significant external funding, industry investment and collaborative research opportunities. Develop and strengthen strategic partnerships with Cisco, healthcare organisations and government stakeholders. Influence policy, strategy and innovation in AI-driven healthcare transformation. Lead curriculum innovation, executive education and industry engagement activities in AI for health systems. Mentor researchers, supervise higher degree research students and contribute to building capability across the sector. Represent the Cisco-La Trobe partnership nationally and internationally through industry forums, conferences, innovation showcases and strategic engagements. Skills and knowledge: A PhD, or equivalent professional standing and recognised expertise in AI, digital health, healthcare systems or a closely related discipline. A strong reputation for translating research, technology or innovation into measurable real-world impact. Demonstrated success building strategic partnerships across academia, healthcare, industry and government. A proven track record securing significant industry investment, research funding, grants or commercial partnerships. Experience leading multidisciplinary teams and large-scale collaborative initiatives. A passion for innovation, research translation and improving healthcare outcomes through emerging technologies. Outstanding stakeholder engagement and influencing skills, with the ability to operate credibly at executive and board level. Please refer to the position description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. Welcome to Bundoora campus – Please click on the video link below: https://f.io/KDo0ceng Benefits 17% superannuation Private Health Insurance discount Plus, many more, click HERE How to apply *Please note, only candidates who possess the full rights to work in Australia will be eligible for consideration for this opportunity*. Closing date: Tuesday 6 th October, 2026 at 11:55pm Position Enquiries: Professor Wenny Rahayu, Dean of School of Computing, Engineering and Mathematical Sciences, Email: W.Rahayu@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Vicki Stavrou, Senior Talent Partner, Strategy and Senior Appointments Email: v.stavrou@latrobe.edu.au Position Description and Booklet below: PD-CISCO Chair for AI Health Systems.pdf Cisco_Chair_AI_Health_Systems_Booklet_SCEMS.pdf Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: Cover letter; An up-to-date resume and Address the Key Selection Criteria We’d love to stay connected! If you would like to find out more about this School, please follow us on LinkedIn: School of Computing, Engineering and Mathematical Sciences: https://www.linkedin.com/company/82850345 Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005 .  If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 07/9/2026 Closing Date: 06/10/2026 Back to search results Apply now Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Job Location Date Closes Cisco Chair for AI in Health Systems Melbourne (Bundoora) 6 Oct 2026 Drive the University's leadership in AI-enabled health systems by fostering world-class research, innovation, and strategic partnerships that transform healthcare delivery and support the implementation of the University's AI First strategy. General Expressions Of Interest Casual Instructional Coaching Role – Momentum CoachED program Join the Momentum CoachED program as an instructional coach, providing one-on-one support that helps teachers strengthen practice and improve student learning. More details... Senior Officer, Customer Care (ASK La Trobe) Work collaboratively within the team and as a member of the ASK La Trobe to facilitate efficient and effective customer service delivery to students and administrative support staff in the University. More details... Casual Campaign - Student Ambassador ASK La Trobe Support new students by answering study and campus enquiries, assisting with orientation planning, providing LMS and Handbook guidance, making referrals, and handling inbound and outbound student communications. More details... Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest Indigenous Australian candidates; register your Expression of Interest here to receive regular job vacancy information at La Trobe University. More details... Current Opportunities Job Closes Cisco Chair for AI in Health Systems 6 Oct 2026 Drive the University's leadership in AI-enabled health systems by fostering world-class research, innovation, and strategic partnerships that transform healthcare delivery and support the implementation of the University's AI First strategy. Powered by PageUp To perform a job search, select your preferred job criteria below. Job search Work Type Fixed Term 1 Location Australia Melbourne (Bundoora) 1 Category Academic Computer Science & IT 1 Computing Engineering & Mathematical Sciences 1 Research 1 Classification Level - Academic Level D - Research Only 1 Want to know more? Recruitment contacts T: +61 (0)3 9479 1234 F: +61 (0)3 9471 0369 Jobs for students Jobs for staff [Restricted] Facebook Twitter Youtube Linked in Instagram Emergency information Contacts Site map Accessibility Privacy Copyright and disclaimer © Copyright 2014 La Trobe University. All rights reserved. CRICOS Provider Code: VIC 00115M"
